                <pb facs="0514" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg480"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 291.</note>
                <head>Mr. Motley to Mr.
                        Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 345.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-06-02"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi>
                            2, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Referring to your No. 186, I have the honor
                    to send herewith copies of a letter and of accompanying documents recently
                    received by me from Lord Clarendon, in relation to the alleged persecution of
                    native converts to Christianity in Japan by the authorities of that empire.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN LOTHROP MOTLEY.</signed></closer>














